# ri_vault/.gitignore
#
# This repo exists to sync the knowledge control plane between two machines:
#   home      — can't query Databricks (stale auth); consumes the committed snapshot
#   work      — can query Databricks live; produces and commits the snapshot
#
# The one thing that CANNOT be regenerated on home is the Databricks grounding, so
# `derived/databricks/` is COMMITTED and is the whole reason this repo syncs.
# Everything else is either hand-curated (tracked) or regenerated from the source
# repos / the committed snapshot (ignored below).

# ── Regenerable derived artifacts (never a committed artifact) ──────────────
# Per-source graphify extracts — the intermediate inputs to the merged graph.
# Rebuilt by scripts/build_graph.py from the source repos; ~1.4M of machine-local
# noise. The merged result lives in graphify-out/ (also ignored).
/derived/sources/

# The unified graph + its cache — regenerated by `refresh` on every machine
# (code-only on home, live on the work laptop). "Regenerated on demand;
# disposable" per CLAUDE.md's layer table, so it is not committed.
# (If you'd rather the query index sync instead of rebuilding, delete the
#  /graphify-out/ line below and add  /graphify-out/cache/  in its place.)
/graphify-out/

# ── Python / tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
coverage.xml
.coverage

# ── OS / editor cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# ── What IS committed (for reference, nothing is ignored here) ──────────────
#   CLAUDE.md
#   config/            sources.yaml + databricks.env (no secrets — profile name only)
#   scripts/           refresh / build_graph / databricks_ground / reconcile / migrate
#   .claude/commands/  refresh · query · reconcile · status · file
#   curated/           the migrated "why" notes
#   contracts/        producer→consumer schema bindings (the join layer)
#   derived/databricks/  the committed snapshot (work produces, home consumes)
#   Inbox/            raw capture, drained by /file
config/sources.local.yaml
